    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena folded a ribbon into 4 equal parts and marked 1/4 on a number line.\n\"One quarter is the unit,\" she said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "fractional unit",
     "equal share",
     "number line"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A fractional unit is one equal part of a whole, such as 1/4. Counting these units gives other fractions: 3 units of 1/4 make 3/4.\nOn a number line from 0 to 1 divide the space into equal parts. Each mark is a multiple of the unit. 1/2 is halfway.\nWe can also measure lengths using fractional units like a quarter metre."
    }
   },
